{{ 'line-template.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  Alterpop — Line header. Source of truth: Wireframe 9b (Line Page).
  Renders on templates/collection.line.json (a collection whose
  templateSuffix is "line", written by the sync app at create/update time
  and only above the 3-piece threshold).

  Data moved from page.* to collection.* (Phase 5 rework):
    H1                  -> collection.title
    manufacturer        -> collection.metafields.alterpop.manufacturer  (BLOCKED -> slot collapses)
    editorial paragraph -> collection.metafields.alterpop.editorial     (BLOCKED -> slot collapses)
    piece count         -> collection.products_count  (live, computable)
    grid / filters / sort -> main-collection-product-grid (Dawn + Search & Discovery)

  Breadcrumb "Lines" is a plain label, not a link — no Lines index page
  exists and Shopify does not expose a /lines/ route root, so the wireframe
  /lines/grandista is not buildable; the real route is /collections/{handle}.

  Interim breadcrumb (Phase 5 addendum): Home > Lines > [Line]. "Home" links
  to routes.root_url and is always present. "Lines" stays a fixed label —
  it is what the wireframe's Universe level collapses to until bl_7 (the
  field linking a Line collection to its parent Universe) exists. NEVER
  derive the Universe from tags/title/cross-collection membership — that is
  inference. Once bl_7 lands, "Lines" is replaced by the real Universe,
  linked to its Universe Room, and the middle crumb below is the place to
  wire it in (kept collapsed, no placeholder — a breadcrumb never shows
  "[ universe ]").

  The 3+ pieces rule is the sync app's: it only creates the collection above
  the threshold. The theme renders what exists and never hides a collection
  by count (that would be inference). Empty collection -> Dawn's default
  empty state via the product grid; this header still renders (title, count 0).

  EMPTY-SLOT INSTRUMENTATION (spec: "estados vazios"). Every slot carries
  data-ap-slot; an empty one carries data-ap-empty for auditing (dev/QA
  signal only — no visible placeholder text reaches the storefront, per
  the 2026-09-15 briefing's global "no [ placeholder ] to the customer" rule).
  Both manufacturer and editorial slots collapse entirely when blank.

  Enters with the shared editorial animation (ap-editorial-in, 400ms;
  neutralised under prefers-reduced-motion in tokens.css).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign manufacturer = collection.metafields.alterpop.manufacturer.value
  assign editorial = collection.metafields.alterpop.editorial.value
  assign piece_count = collection.products_count
-%}

<section class="ap-line-header" aria-label="{{ collection.title | escape }}">
  <div class="ap-line-header__inner page-width">
    <nav class="ap-line-header__crumbs type-caption" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">{{ 'sections.catalogue.home' | t }}</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span>
      {%- comment -%}
        Universe level — BLOCKED (bl_7). Collapses to the fixed "Lines"
        label until collection.metafields.alterpop.universe exists; then
        swap for a link to the Universe Room. Never derive it from tags,
        title, or cross-collection membership.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign ap_universe = collection.metafields.alterpop.universe.value -%}
      {%- if ap_universe != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ ap_universe.url }}">{{ ap_universe.title | escape }}</a>
      {%- else -%}
        <span>{{ 'sections.catalogue.lines' | t }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      <span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span>
      <span aria-current="page">{{ collection.title | escape }}</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="ap-line-header__title type-display">{{ collection.title | escape | upcase }}</h1>

    {%- if manufacturer != blank -%}
      <p class="ap-line-header__manufacturer type-body" data-ap-slot="manufacturer">
        {{ manufacturer | escape }}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div
      class="ap-line-header__editorial type-body rte"
      data-ap-slot="editorial"
      {% if editorial == blank %}data-ap-empty{% endif %}
    >
      {%- if editorial != blank -%}{{ editorial }}{%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <p class="ap-line-header__meta type-caption" data-ap-slot="products-count">
      {{ 'sections.catalogue.count_pieces' | t: count: piece_count }}
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Line header",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [],
  "enabled_on": { "templates": ["collection"] }
}
{% endschema %}
